        "provenance": "doccloakModified",
        "status": "active"
      },
      "description": "International phone number with + prefix (Docudis changes: 2026-09-18 no line break inside the number, it used to take the first digits of a postcode or a year on the next line; 2026-09-23 a lone \"t\" right before the digits counts as the +, iOS OCR read \"+44 7700 900123\" as \"t447700 900123\")",
      "examples": [
        "+1 (555) 123-4567",
        "+48 600 123 456",
        "+44 20 7946 0958",
        "t447700 900123"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "regex:universal:iban",
      "entityType": "IBAN",
      "pattern": "\\b[A-Z]{2}[ \\u00A0]?\\d{2}[ \\u00A0]?[A-Z\\d \\u00A0]{10,30}\\b",
      "flags": "g",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "domains": [
        "financial"
      ],
      "classification": {
        "category": "financialAccount",
        "subtype": "iban",
        "applicability": "baseline",
        "verticals": [
          "finance"
        ],
        "protectionLevel": "essential",
        "defaultAction": "hide",
        "provenance": "doccloakModified",
        "status": "active"
      },
      "description": "IBAN (2-letter country code + 2 check digits + up to 30 alphanumeric). Docudis change 2026-09-21: the separator class was \\s, which includes the newline, so an IBAN at the end of a line ran on into the uppercase word starting the next one (\"…7536 63\nBIC\"). The mod-97 check then failed and the whole IBAN went undetected, leaving it to the loose long-number rule, which covered only the digits and left the country and bank code in plain sight.",
      "examples": [
        "GB29 NWBK 6016 1331 9268 19",
        "DE89 3704 0044 0532 0130 00",
        "PL61 1090 1014 0000 0712 1981 2874"
      ],
      "validate": "ibanMod97"
    },
    {
      "id": "regex:universal:iban_masked",
      "entityType": "IBAN",
      "pattern": "\\b[A-Z]{2}[ \\u00A0]?\\d{2}(?=[ \\u00A0A-Z\\d*x]{0,40}[*x])(?:[ \\u00A0]?[A-Z\\d*x]{2,6}){2,8}",
      "flags": "gu",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "domains": [
        "financial"
      ],
      "classification": {
        "category": "financialAccount",
        "subtype": "masked_iban",
        "applicability": "baseline",
        "verticals": [
          "finance"
        ],
        "protectionLevel": "essential",
        "defaultAction": "hide",
        "provenance": "docudis",
        "status": "active"
      },
      "description": "Part-masked IBAN, \"ES90 8200 **** **** **** 4820\" (Docudis addition 2026-09-21). The validated iban rule cannot see these: masking characters break the mod-97 check, so a statement that stars out the middle of its own IBAN left the country, bank and last four digits in plain sight.",
      "examples": [
        "ES90 8200 **** **** **** 4820",
        "FR76 8457 **** **** **** **31 349"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "regex:universal:masked_account",
      "entityType": "OTHER",
      "pattern": "(?<![\\w*])[xX*]{4,}[ \\u00A0-]?\\d{3,6}\\b",
